From d61045e623eb4ced972a4c091268b82129ffdd7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:19:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] A limb moves through its keys on a curve, not from key to key
 in straight lines (patch 0076)

1.12's character clips are keyed sparsely and played linearly, so a limb snaps from pose to pose
with a kink in its motion at every key. While the action layer is live, the evaluator now samples
each translation and rotation on a curve through the keys: a cubic Hermite with monotone tangents
(per axis, the harmonic mean of the slopes on either side of a key, and nothing where the motion
turns back). It passes through every key exactly and carries one speed across it, and it never
overshoots a key or bulges through a held pose, so an impact frame lands where it is keyed and a
hold stays held. A turn takes the same curve in its log space about the segment's first key.

`PoseTrack::sample` stays Bevy's exact linear and slerp (the oracle tests compare it key for key);
the curve is `PoseTrack::sample_smooth`. It runs while an add-on drives the action layer and
`actionCurves` (benilla's own, registered "1") is on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
